  "factor_name": "Benchmark-Residual Risk-Adjusted Reversal 40D",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "-rolling_sum_40(residual_return) / (rolling_std_40(residual_return)*sqrt(40)+epsilon), lagged 1 day",
    "description": "For each tradable instrument, estimate a rolling 120-day beta to the equal-weight mean return of the 15 tradable instruments. Form the asset return residual after removing beta times the benchmark return. Fade the 40-day cumulative residual move, normalized by its 40-day residual volatility. The one-day lag ensures only completed data are used."
  },
